    "basis": [
      "jinshu:053:s0034–s0035 and zizhitongjian:083:s0128–s0129 give the same proposed 韓壽女 marriage, the prince’s desire for a Han alliance, and refusal by 壽妻賈午 and the empress. Name plus wife and daughter in this distinctive failed betrothal identify the same Han Shou across these two members.",
      "jinshu:031:s0571 and zizhitongjian:083:s0159 explicitly name 妹夫韓壽 and his son 慰祖 whom the empress takes and raises for substitution as heir. This shared named son, brother-in-law relation and adoption/substitution episode connects the other two members to Jia Wu’s husband. The full governing contexts place these retrospective episodes within the same empress’s household, without an alternative Han Shou."
    ],
